{"title":"2003 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/2/2a230e9e7115f0bd96711a39650ff2e6e272a985.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K, L, M,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"67\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> lie in the plane of the square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/2/a42a626828b86fa849503f4f5dc2519147308dfd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AKB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54df32ebbe6c4f6c4493d8531ec0ef1937ed7dbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BLC$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3f7db9e5618aa83bb58ddccac7693cf92a75d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CMD$\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/4/4d47f702cf57821a24badb53da336d10a027aca6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DNA$\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" /> are equilateral triangles. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> has an area of 16, find the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/b/c8baa210c35a8d98d01f9f4d4c956c5a7bcd15ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KLMN$\" width=\"65\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/0/14057a8f4f08bad17471fdaed56a758f1e2fcea7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(2cm); defaultpen(fontsize(8)+linewidth(0.8)); pair A=(-0.5,0.5), B=(0.5,0.5), C=(0.5,-0.5), D=(-0.5,-0.5); pair K=(0,1.366), L=(1.366,0), M=(0,-1.366), N=(-1.366,0); draw(A--N--K--A--B--K--L--B--C--L--M--C--D--M--N--D--A); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,SE); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,SW); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,NW); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,NE); label(&quot;$K$&quot;,K,NNW); label(&quot;$L$&quot;,L,E); label(&quot;$M$&quot;,M,S); label(&quot;$N$&quot;,N,W); [/asy]\" width=\"295\" height=\"288\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/3/5d3e2552e9bcb332d6f073db2a58513e3a67f65f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textrm{(A)}\\ 32\\qquad\\textrm{(B)}\\ 16+16\\sqrt{3}\\qquad\\textrm{(C)}\\ 48\\qquad\\textrm{(D)}\\ 32+16\\sqrt{3}\\qquad\\textrm{(E)}\\ 64$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"505\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Since the area of square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/d/63d6c106db68e00b44df7f3172065e1079a703af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ABCD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" /> is 16, the side length must be 4. Thus, the side length of triangle AKB is 4, and the height of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/e/0eeabcf5e6c486a928bd172cdb51948a67571656.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{AKB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"13\" />, and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/a/29a58b2432577d411e5873a31c9849ec02287b8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{DMC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/5/e455d80f4657b1112ba302a6e2c42e9c81f780ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>The diagonal of the square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/c/c6c7af1c8c923b1b7379a2760a001b59e2f196a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{KNML}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"13\" /> will then be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/f/91fe377b3152f390001b2ab87f24a32ff559073b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4+4\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />. From here there are 2 ways to proceed:\n</p><p>First: Since the diagonal is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/f/91fe377b3152f390001b2ab87f24a32ff559073b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4+4\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />, the side length is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/1/2e1fcdc1c674ec6183d95537a823acac81d5ede7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4+4\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"67\" height=\"45\" />, and the area is thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/4/9e4b1ef1f47fe74e864801c06ae48863cfc73331.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{16+48+32\\sqrt{3}}{2}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 32+16\\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"283\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>Second: Since a square is a rhombus, the area of the square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/2/1a2db988959c34f6006b7b0e0baddf48f8601fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{d_1d_2}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"36\" height=\"37\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/6/44612d9d6ec37da7f4edd0f205d65cdac5954dc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/7/117778db99ba8932dc35128d085c2619f4f690a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> are the diagonals of the rhombus. Since the diagonal is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/f/91fe377b3152f390001b2ab87f24a32ff559073b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4+4\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />, the area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/7/a47c8a12b6a3dbcaf1a47ab24a864748b8a0ee85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(4+4\\sqrt{3})^2}{2}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 32+16\\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"246\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> has area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, its side length is simply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/f/ccfdc8810c791453a7a0d927240385d31e08689e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{16}\\implies 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"92\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Angle chasing, we find that the angle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/8/e689cb93d82dd98c66e9e16601cd596892dbbdf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KBL=360-(90+2(60))=360-(210)=150$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"379\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>We also know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e9025ebfdbc4b21e7d19f6e45f1cd88efeb811e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KB=4, BL=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"133\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Using Law of Cosines, we find that side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/8/6a830bb972f32308de1615d2b45e2dd91548c4de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(KL)^2=16+16-2(16)cos{150}\\implies (KL)^2=32+\\frac{32\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\implies (KL)^2=32+16\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"668\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>However, the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/b/c8baa210c35a8d98d01f9f4d4c956c5a7bcd15ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KLMN$\" width=\"65\" height=\"12\" /> is simply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/2/0c25c637a914e945fe05566b55c2afa8d2356f75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(KL)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"19\" />, hence the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b42cc159405319d9c4090a5368c38fd9a333a21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 32+16\\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"132\" height=\"35\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>First we show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/b/c8baa210c35a8d98d01f9f4d4c956c5a7bcd15ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KLMN$\" width=\"65\" height=\"12\" /> is a square. How? Show that it is a rhombus that has a right angle.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/6/a860cbacb852418c3441c879c75315c8b93b89fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{NAK}=\\angle{KBL}=\\angle{LCM}=\\angle{DNM}=150^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"374\" height=\"15\" />. All the sides of the equilateral triangles are equal, so the triangles are congruent. Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/e/0ee72a561a6cddf7e6327cdc05e4b472608fd49f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{KNL}=45^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"110\" height=\"15\" />, etc, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/f/0cf3e6b03d9d5289590935b373ce09d97160933b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{KNM}=90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"118\" height=\"15\" />. So we have a square.\n</p><p>Instead of going to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/b/15b902cd5392b3e4bbda5878d8ae7f99eb8291eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KN$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> using Law of Cosines, we can inscribe the square in another bigger one and then subtract the four right triangles in the corners, so after all of this, we find that the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b42cc159405319d9c4090a5368c38fd9a333a21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 32+16\\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"132\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p>~hastapasta (edited)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A\" title=\"2003 AMC 12A\">2003 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2003 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2003 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2003 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2003 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2003 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2003 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2003 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2003 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2003 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2003 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2003 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2003 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2003 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2003 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2003 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2003 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2003 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2003 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2003 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2003 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2003 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2003 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2003 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2003 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2003 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2003 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2003 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2003 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017201829\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.064 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.083 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 303/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2298/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7833/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   17.756      1 -total\n 59.43%   10.552      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 37.07%    6.583      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:9013:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017201829 and revision id 194696. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}